/// Term 5: "Numbers to 100 and Repeated Addition" (Weeks 17-20)
/// continues Year 1 Mathematics's pathway, extending Term 1 Week 1's
/// "ten and some more" framing (previously only 11-19, one ten) to the
/// full 1-100 range with multiple whole tens: Week 17 counts in tens up
/// to 100; Week 18 breaks any two-digit number into its tens and ones
/// and extends Term 1 Week 2's ordering/comparing skill from 1-20 to the
/// fuller 1-100 range; Week 19 introduces repeated addition (equal
/// groups) as a genuinely new concept -- adding the SAME number several
/// times, distinct from Term 2's addition of two different numbers;
/// Week 20 is the capstone, combining all three into one real-world
/// scenario. No multiplication symbol, times-tables, or division is
/// introduced -- repeated addition stays a horizontal addition number
/// sentence throughout, matching this pathway's age-appropriate-methods
/// discipline.
