/// Term 5 ("Fractions") of the Year 4 Mathematics pathway -- a return to
/// number work after Term 4's measurement breadth strand. Week 17 opens
/// the fractions strand: naming fractions as equal parts of a whole or a
/// group, identifying the numerator and denominator, and the requirement
/// that parts be truly equal before a fraction name applies; Week 18
/// introduces equivalent fractions (multiplying/dividing numerator and
/// denominator by the same number) and simplifying; Week 19 introduces
/// comparing and ordering same-denominator fractions, and adding/
/// subtracting same-denominator fractions; Week 20 closes the term with a
/// capstone -- a single "Nova School Bake Sale" scenario requiring
/// naming fractions, equivalent fractions, AND comparing/adding same-
/// denominator fractions together, reusing every skill from Weeks 17-19.
/// Content was authored by four parallel worktree-isolated agents (one
/// per week) and independently re-verified end to end (every fraction
/// fact, equivalence, comparison, and addition/subtraction) before being
/// spliced in here.
