      xpReward: 10,
      readingPassage: ReadingPassageModel(
        titleEn: "Zin Min and the Nova School Building & Design Fair",
        titleMy: "ဇင်မင်းနှင့် Nova ကျောင်း တည်ဆောက်ရေးနှင့် ဒီဇိုင်းပြပွဲ",
        passageEn:
            "At the end of Term 6, Nova School holds its first Building & Design Fair, where every Year 5 student designs a mini blueprint for a dream clubhouse. Zin Min starts by drawing her clubhouse floor plan on grid paper, using her Week 21 conversion skills to make sure every measurement on her blueprint is in the same unit, converting a wall length from 2.5 m into 250 cm to match the rest of her plan.\n\nNext, Zin Min calculates how much wood trim she needs to go around the edge of her rectangular clubhouse floor, which is 6 m long and 4 m wide. Remembering her Week 22 perimeter skill, she uses 2 x (length + width) to find that she needs 20 m of wood trim in total. She then uses her Week 23 area skill to calculate that the floor itself covers 24 square metres, enough space for a reading corner and a small table.\n\nFinally, Zin Min designs a cuboid-shaped storage box for the clubhouse, 3 m long, 2 m wide, and 2 m high, and uses her volume formula to find it can hold 12 cubic metres of space for books and games. At the fair, judges are impressed that Zin Min combined unit conversion, perimeter, area, and volume all in one blueprint. Her clubhouse design wins the \"Most Complete Blueprint\" award, celebrating everything she learned across Term 6.",
        passageMy:
