      titleEn: "Reading: Kaung Htet's Snack Stall Puzzle",
      titleMy: "စာဖတ်ခြင်း — ကောင်းထက်၏ သရေစာဆိုင် ပဟေဠိ",
      kind: LessonKind.reading,
      xpReward: 10,
      readingPassage: ReadingPassageModel(
        titleEn: "Kaung Htet's Snack Stall Puzzle",
        titleMy: "ကောင်းထက်၏ သရေစာဆိုင် ပဟေဠိ",
        passageEn:
            "Kaung Htet was running the snack stall for his class's annual fun fair, and by the end of the morning he had two receipts but had lost track of the individual prices. The first receipt showed that 4 samosas and 3 cups of tea together cost 2400 kyats. The second receipt showed that 4 samosas and 5 cups of tea together cost 3200 kyats. Kaung Htet wanted to know the price of one samosa and one cup of tea, so he set up two simultaneous equations: 4x + 3y = 2400 and 4x + 5y = 3200, where x was the price of a samosa and y was the price of a cup of tea. Looking closely, he noticed the x-coefficients were already matching -- both equations had 4x, and both were the same sign. That meant he could eliminate x simply by subtracting the first equation from the second. Subtracting gave him (4x + 5y) - (4x + 3y) = 3200 - 2400, which simplified to 2y = 800, so y = 400. A cup of tea cost 400 kyats. Substituting y = 400 back into the first equation, he calculated 4x + 3(400) = 2400, so 4x = 2400 - 1200 = 1200, giving x = 300. A samosa cost 300 kyats. To be sure, Kaung Htet checked his answers in the second equation too: 4(300) + 5(400) = 1200 + 2000 = 3200, which matched perfectly. His elimination method had worked.",
        passageMy:
