        passageEn:
            "Yoon Nandar wanted to buy a storybook that cost 12,000 kyats. She already had 3,000 kyats saved in her piggy bank, and her grandmother agreed to give her 1,500 kyats every week for helping in the garden. Yoon Nandar wondered how many weeks she would need to save enough money.\n\nShe wrote an inequality to describe her savings. If w stands for the number of weeks, her total savings after w weeks would be 3000 + 1500w kyats. She needed this amount to be at least 12,000 kyats, so she wrote: 3000 + 1500w ≥ 12000.\n\nTo solve it, she subtracted 3000 from both sides: 1500w ≥ 9000. Then she divided both sides by 1500, and because 1500 is a positive number, the inequality sign stayed the same: w ≥ 6.\n\nYoon Nandar smiled. She needed at least 6 weeks of helping in the garden. She drew a number line to show her answer. Because the inequality included 'or equal to,' she drew a closed circle at 6 and shaded the line to the right, showing that 6, 7, 8, and every week after would also work.\n\nHer older brother, who was studying graphs at school, told her that if they plotted the same relationship as y ≥ 1500x + 3000 on a graph, they would draw a solid boundary line, since the inequality was not strict. Yoon Nandar was proud that her careful weeks of gardening would finally pay off.",
