const CoursePathwayDef year3MathematicsPathway = CoursePathwayDef(
  id: "course-year3-mathematics",
  subject: "mathematics",
  grade: Grade.year3,
  titleEn: "Mathematics — Year 3 Course",
  titleMy: "သင်္ချာ — တတိယတန်း သင်တန်း",
  descriptionEn:
      "The Year 3 Mathematics course follows Kaung Sett, a Nova School student, across a full academic year. Term 1, Numbers to 1,000, covers hundreds/tens/ones place value, comparing and ordering numbers up to 1,000, and rounding to the nearest 10 and 100, closing with a Founders' Day Fair capstone combining every skill in one running fair-stall scenario. Term 2, Adding and Subtracting with Regrouping, covers column addition without and with carrying, and column subtraction with borrowing (including borrowing through zero), closing with a School Book Drive capstone tracking a running total across a week of donations. Term 3, Multiplication and Division Facts, covers equal groups and arrays, the 3 and 4 times tables, and division as sharing or grouping, closing with a Class Party Shop capstone. Term 4, Measurement, covers length (centimetres and metres), mass (grams and kilograms), and capacity (millilitres and litres), closing with a Nova School Fun Fair Measurement Booth capstone combining all three. Term 5, Fractions, covers fractions of a shape, fractions of a set of objects, and comparing and ordering simple fractions, closing with a Pizza Party capstone. Term 6, Time, covers telling time to the nearest 5 minutes, days/weeks/months/years, and elapsed time, closing with a School Day Schedule capstone. Term 7, Shapes and Symmetry, covers 2D shapes, 3D shapes, and lines of symmetry, closing with a Shape Museum capstone. Term 8, Money, covers understanding Kyat notes, adding money, and subtracting money to find change, closing with a School Shop capstone. Term 9, the year-end capstone (\"Year 3 Math Capstone Project: The Nova School Founders' Day Festival\"), is pure review/integration across four weeks: Week 33 reuses Term 1 (numbers to 1,000 and rounding) and Term 3 (multiplication and division facts) for festival planning; Week 34 reuses Term 2 (column addition/subtraction with regrouping) and Term 4 (length, mass, and capacity measurement) for building and measuring the festival booths; Week 35 reuses Term 5 (fractions), Term 6 (time), and Term 7 (shapes and symmetry) for the festival day's activities; and Week 36, the grand finale, reuses Term 8 (money) to close the festival's books and closes the entire 36-week course with a recap naming all 8 earlier terms' contributions.",
  descriptionMy:
